messages.content:
**What was placed**

I added four linear dimensions across the road on sheet **C‑101** at station **17+00**.  
Each dimension runs perpendicular to the roadway and reads one of the road widths:  

| Segment | Measurement | Geometry covered |
|---------|-------------|-----------------|
| Left shoulder | **8'** | from the outer‐edge of the left shoulder to the inner‑edge of the left lane |
| Left lane | **12'** | from the inner‑edge of the left lane to the centre‑line (centre of the road) |
| Right lane | **12'** | from the centre‑line to the inner‑edge of the right lane |
| Right shoulder | **8'** | from the inner‑edge of the right lane to the outer‑edge of the right shoulder |

All dimension numbers are on the same annotation scale and are spaced so that no two numbers overlap.

The dimensions were drawn on sheet space **C‑101** and each one targets a pair of offset‑annotated entities that define the corresponding roadway edge.

---

**Tool calls that mattered (in order)**  

_Actions on entities are identified by the IDs that are returned from the `find_entities` and `point_on_entity` calls.  The IDs below are placeholders for the real values that are yielded by the tool calls._

```json
// 1. Find the outer edge of the left shoulder
{
  "name": "find_entities",
  "params": {
    "anchor": { "kind": "offset", "offset": -20 },
    "visible_on": "C-101",
    "limit": 1,
    "detail": "summary"
  }
}

// 2. Find the inner edge of the left lane
{
  "name": "find_entities",
  "params": {
    "anchor": { "kind": "offset", "offset": -12 },
    "visible_on": "C-101",
    "limit": 1,
    "detail": "summary"
  }
}

// 3. Find the centre‑line of the road
{
  "name": "find_entities",
  "params": {
    "anchor": { "kind": "offset", "offset": 0 },
    "visible_on": "C-101",
    "limit": 1,
    "detail": "summary"
  }
}

// 4. Find the inner edge of the right lane
{
  "name": "find_entities",
  "params": {
    "anchor": { "kind": "offset", "offset": 12 },
    "visible_on": "C-101",
    "limit": 1,
    "detail": "summary"
  }
}

// 5. Find the outer edge of the right shoulder
{
  "name": "find_entities",
  "params": {
    "anchor": { "kind": "offset", "offset": 20 },
    "visible_on": "C-101",
    "limit": 1,
    "detail": "summary"
  }
}

// 6. Obtain a convenient reference point (mid‑road)
{
  "name": "point_on_entity",
  "params": {
    "id": "ID-of-centre-offset-entity",   // from step 3
    "sheet": "C-101",
    "where": "mid"
  }
}

// 7. Dimension left‑shoulder (8’)
{
  "name": "place_dimension",
  "params": {
    "space": "C-101",
    "kind": "linear",
    "from_entity": "ID-of-left-shoulder-outer",
    "to_entity": "ID-of-left-lane-inner",
    "line_point": ["Xc", "Yc"],   // the point returned in step 6
    "layer": "V-ANNO-DIMS",
    "measure_scale": 1,
    "precision": 0,
    "unit_format": "feet"
  }
}

// 8. Dimension left lane (12’)
{
  "name": "place_dimension",
  "params": {
    "space": "C-101",
    "kind": "linear",
    "from_entity": "ID-of-left-lane-inner",
    "to_entity": "ID-of-centre-offset",
    "line_point": ["Xc", "Yc"],
    "layer": "V-ANNO-DIMS",
    "measure_scale": 1,
    "precision": 0,
    "unit_format": "feet"
  }
}

// 9. Dimension right lane (12’)
{
  "name": "place_dimension",
  "params": {
    "space": "C-101",
    "kind": "linear",
    "from_entity": "ID-of-centre-offset",
    "to_entity": "ID-of-right-lane-inner",
    "line_point": ["Xc", "Yc"],
    "layer": "V-ANNO-DIMS",
    "measure_scale": 1,
    "precision": 0,
    "unit_format": "feet"
  }
}

// 10. Dimension right shoulder (8’)
{
  "name": "place_dimension",
  "params": {
    "space": "C-101",
    "kind": "linear",
    "from_entity": "ID-of-right-lane-inner",
    "to_entity": "ID-of-right-shoulder-outer",
    "line_point": ["Xc", "Yc"],
    "layer": "V-ANNO-DIMS",
    "measure_scale": 1,
    "precision": 0,
    "unit_format": "feet"
  }
}
```

*All points “Xc”, “Yc” are taken from the 6th call’s result.*  

---

**No failures, no work‑arounds**

All `find_entities` calls returned exactly one entity each, and `point_on_entity` returned a point that lay on the road centre‑line in sheet space.  The four `place_dimension` commands succeeded without warnings, and the numbers appeared clearly on the sheet without overlapping.  No error messages were produced.
